# Updater environment template
#
# The app needs NO environment variables. `npm run dev` works with this file
# absent: with no sign-in variables set, Updater runs in local mode (one
# workspace in the browser, no account). Only the Google sign-in block below
# is read by the current code; the other entries are reserved for planned
# integrations (see tracker.md, Phase 10) so names stay consistent.
#
# Rules (see rules.md §7.3):
# - Copy to `.env.local` for local values. `.env.local` is git-ignored.
# - Never commit real secrets.
# - Only variables prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_ are exposed to the browser.
#   Never put a credential behind a NEXT_PUBLIC_ name.

# --- Planned: GitHub integration (T10.1, T10.2) — server-only ---
# Optional token to raise the GitHub REST API rate limit for read-only public data.
# GITHUB_TOKEN=
# OAuth app credentials for the future "Connect GitHub" flow.
# GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
# GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- Google sign-in (T10.5) — server-only ---
# Set all three to require a Google sign-in and give each account its own
# workspace. Setting only some of them blocks the app until the rest are set.
# Restart the server after changing them.
#
# Random secret that encrypts the session cookie. Generate one with:
#   openssl rand -base64 33
# AUTH_SECRET=
# OAuth client from Google Cloud Console → APIs & Services → Credentials →
# "OAuth client ID" (type: Web application). Authorized redirect URI:
#   http://localhost:3000/api/auth/callback/google   (development)
#   https://<your-domain>/api/auth/callback/google   (production)
# AUTH_GOOGLE_ID=
# AUTH_GOOGLE_SECRET=
# Self-hosting behind `npm run start` (not Vercel): trust the Host header,
# or set AUTH_URL to the public origin instead.
# AUTH_TRUST_HOST=true
# AUTH_URL=https://<your-domain>

# --- Planned: AI-assisted drafting (T10.7) — server-only, always optional ---
# AI_PROVIDER_API_KEY=
